# Code owners (adopted by Lee, 2026-11-18; working plan section 12, docs/governance/README.md).
#
# GitHub reads this file from .github/, the repository root or docs/, in that order, and uses the first it
# finds. It applies per branch: the file on a pull request's base branch decides the review requests. Every
# owner needs explicit write access. Patterns follow gitignore rules without `!` or `[ ]`; the last matching
# line wins.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# This file only requests reviews. Requiring code-owner review is a separate repository setting; see
# docs/governance/README.md before turning it on while @leenadav is the only owner.
#
# Every line of the file this replaced is kept (the whole tree, /protocol_engine/, /.github/, SECURITY.md,
# THREAT-MODEL.md). Add a second owner per area once Lee names one.

# Default: everything.
*                                   @leenadav

# Python reference engine and adapters: detection behaviour (engine lane).
